{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Custom-Keyboards"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This developer guide describes the iOS keyboard extension model."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Developer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Dictation","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-dSYMs","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Memory-Management","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Themes"],"title":"Developer"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-custom-keyboards"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is an app extension that you ship with your app. Once enabled, it can replace the system keyboard by selecting it with the 🌐 key while typing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyboard extensions are the only kind of apps that can be used directly with other apps in iOS. By extending your app’s features for use in a custom iOS keyboard, your users will be able to use them in any app that supports text input."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"How-can-I-create-a-custom-keyboard","text":"How can I create a custom keyboard?","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can add a custom keyboard extension to any iOS app, from Xcode’s “File > New > Target…” menu option. This will add a keyboard extension to your app and make it possible to switch to that keyboard while typing in any app."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"this article","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for a guide on how to create a custom keyboard extension from scratch, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/library\/archive\/documentation\/General\/Conceptual\/ExtensibilityPG\/CustomKeyboard.html"},{"text":" for more extensive information.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"How-can-a-user-select-my-keyboard","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"How can a user select my keyboard?"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Users can enable more keyboards in Settings, under “General > Keyboard > Keyboards > Add New Keyboard”. Once the keyboard has been added, the user can also enable “Full Access”, which is required for advanced system access.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-be-used-for","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What can a custom keyboard be used for?"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom keyboard can be used to provide additional typing support, more sophisticated text analysis, bring AI-support directly to the user input experience, etc. The possibilities are endless, but Apple’s native APIs are very limited by default.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-do","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What can a custom keyboard do?"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A custom keyboard can render any user interface and resize the keyboard area to fit its content. It uses a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"document proxy"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to read and write text from and to the currnetly active text field, and can require Full Access to enable capabilities like network access."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"What can a custom keyboard NOT do?","level":2,"anchor":"What-can-a-custom-keyboard-NOT-do"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple’s native APIs are very limited, and basically just lets you read and write text. Some things are however not possible. For instance, a custom keyboard can’t draw outside its bounds, and is memory capped to ~70 MB. Apple also doesn’t provide a default keyboard view."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Why should I use KeyboardKit?","type":"heading","anchor":"Why-should-I-use-KeyboardKit"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit supports 100+ languages and extends Apple’s native APIs with more features to make it a easier to create amazing custom keyboards. KeyboardKit also has a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" that renders a fully customizable keyboard with just a few lines of code."}]},{"text":"Further Reading","anchor":"Further-Reading","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"overridingTitle":"this article","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/documentation\/uikit\/creating-a-custom-keyboard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for a guide on how to create a custom keyboard extension from scratch, and "},{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this article"}],"overridingTitle":"this article","identifier":"https:\/\/developer.apple.com\/library\/archive\/documentation\/General\/Conceptual\/ExtensibilityPG\/CustomKeyboard.html","isActive":true,"type"